@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Account API
	Testing Koroneiki Account API functionality.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Automotive |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Digital Experience Platform |
	| Liferay Portal Six                  |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Default Account Role |
	| Extra Account Role   |

Scenario: Create and view account with nested fields
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Koroneiki accounts created with nested fields via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact2                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                      |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the extra role for accounts |
	| Name        | Extra Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Worker                      |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a nested field for the contact role with the name "Default Account Role"
	And I rename the first contact role nested field variable
	And I create a nested field for the contact role with the name "Extra Account Role"
	And I rename the second contact role nested field variable
	And I create a nested field for the customer contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the contact roles nested field value "${staticContactRolesNestedField1}"
	And I rename the first contact nested field variable
	And I create a nested field for the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the contact roles nested field value "${staticContactRolesNestedField2}"
	And I rename the second contact nested field variable
	And I create a nested field for the account external link with the following values 
	| Domain      | koroneikiautomotive |
	| Entity Id   | 1234                |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiAutomotive |
	And I create a nested field for the postal address with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 91761           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 123 Fake Street |
	And I create a nested field for the product purchase external link with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxppurchase |
	| Entity Id   | 12345              |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXPPurchase |
	And I create a nested field for the product purchase for the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| End Date                   | ${staticEndDate}                                 |                |
	| External Link Nested Field | ${staticProductPurchaseExternalLinksNestedField} |                |
	| Original End Date          | ${staticOriginalEndDate}                         |                |
	| Perpetual                  | false                                            |                |
	| Product Field and Value    | additionalProp1                                  | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value    | additionalProp3                                  | propertyValue3 |
	| Product Field and Value    | additionalProp2                                  | propertyValue2 |
	| Quantity                   | 1                                                |                |
	| Start Date                 | ${staticStartDate}                               |                |
	| Status                     | Approved                                         |                |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                          | KORAUTO                                                     | |
	| Contact Nested Field          | ${staticContactsNestedField1},${staticContactsNestedField2} | |
	| Description                   | Test automotive account on koroneiki                        | |
	| External Link Nested Field    | ${staticAccountExternalLinksNestedField}                    | |
	| Fax Number                    | 555-555-1234                                                | |
	| Name                          | Koroneiki Automotive                                        | |
	| Phone Number                  | 555-555-5678                                                | |
	| Postal Address Nested Field   | ${staticPostalAddressesNestedField}                         | |
	| Product Purchase Nested Field | ${staticProductPurchasesNestedField}                        | |
	| Profile Email Address         | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken                    | |
	| Region                        | United States                                               | |
	| Status                        | Active                                                      | |
	| Tier                          | T4                                                          | |
	| Website                       | www.koroneikiautomotive.com                                 | |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the following values
	| Code                          | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Customer Contact Nested Field | ${staticContactsNestedField1}            | |
	| Description                   | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| External Link Nested Field    | ${staticAccountExternalLinksNestedField} | |
	| Fax Number                    | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                          | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number                  | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Postal Address Nested Field   | ${staticPostalAddressesNestedField}      | |
	| Product Purchase Nested Field | ${staticProductPurchasesNestedField}     | |
	| Profile Email Address         | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                        | United States                            | |
	| Status                        | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                          | T4                                       | |
	| Website                       | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	| Worker Contact Nested Field   | ${staticContactsNestedField2}            | |
	And the customer contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the customer contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Default Account Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"
	And the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the worker contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Extra Account Role"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the contact role "Member"
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Koroneiki Automotive" for the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |                |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |                |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1          | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3          | propertyValue3 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2          | propertyValue2 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |                |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |                |
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Koroneiki Automotive" for the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" via nested field with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |                |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |                |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1          | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3          | propertyValue3 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2          | propertyValue2 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |                |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |                |
	And the external link with the entity id "12345" should be present on the product purchase made by account "Koroneiki Automotive" for the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxppurchase |
	| Entity Id   | 12345              |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXPPurchase |
	And the external link with the entity id "12345" should be present on the product purchase made by account "Koroneiki Automotive" for the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" via the external link key with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxppurchase |
	| Entity Id   | 12345              |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXPPurchase |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikiautomotive |
	| Entity Id   | 1234                |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiAutomotive |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" via the external link key with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikiautomotive |
	| Entity Id   | 1234                |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiAutomotive |
	And I should be able to view a postal address on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the street address "123 Fake Street" with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 91761           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 123 Fake Street |

